# Line-ending and encoding policy.
#
# This repository lives on a file share used from both Windows and macOS, and
# is edited by more than one person and more than one agent. Without explicit
# rules, `core.autocrlf` differs per machine and every checkout produces
# whole-file diffs that bury the real change.
#
# Rule: LF in the repository, LF in the working tree, everywhere.
#
# This is the public mirror, so the cost of getting it wrong is higher than
# noise: a whole-file reformat pushed to GitHub is visible forever, and it
# hides the one-line driver change it was carrying.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf

# Driver definitions are authored, already stored with LF, and parsed happily
# that way by TestController - `#eol` sets protocol framing on the wire, not
# the line endings of the file. No `-text` exception, deliberately.

# Binary assets - Setup dialog screenshots
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
